## Step 3: Assess Validation Status

**18-15deg-600s-NoN2 (run3):** This is the highest PF point (0.44) on the Pareto front. Run1 had a top-edge gap defect. Run2 had E=340, PF=0.32 (poor). Run3 had E=421, PF=0.44 with good quality. This is a large apparent gain in PF with only one good measurement — needs validation.

**17p5-15deg-60s-N2:** Three runs with E=520/696/407 and PF=0.36/0.26/0.32 — highly variable. Run2 had the highest E but lowest PF; run1 had best balanced performance. Not reproducibly confirmed.

**17p5-19deg-90s-N2:** Two runs: E=861/PF=0.28 and E=549/PF=0.30. Inconsistent modulus. Not confirmed.

