## Step 2: Identify the Pareto Front (maximize both E and PF)

A point is non-dominated if no other point has both higher E and higher PF.

Key candidates to check:
- **18-0add-15deg-600s-NoN2-1350s run3**: E=421, PF=0.44 — high PF
- **19p5-0add-25deg-130s-NoN2-1550s run1**: E=351, PF=0.43 — dominated by run3 on both
- **17p5-0add-20deg-90s-N2-1250s run4**: E=502, PF=0.35
- **17p5-0add-20deg-90s-N2-1250s run5**: E=530, PF=0.34
- **17-0add-10deg-60s-N2-1800s**: E=382, PF=0.36 — dominated by run4 (502>382, 0.35~0.36 close)
- **17-0add-18deg-90s-N2-1800s run2**: E=454, PF=0.33
- **17p5-0add-16deg-75s-N2-1800s**: E=697, PF=0.32
- **17p5-0add-18deg-75s-N2-1800s run2**: E=675, PF=0.30
- **17p5-0add-19deg-90s-N2-1800s**: E=861, PF=0.28 — high E, lower PF
- **17p5-0add-5deg-550s-N2-1450s run1**: E=778, PF=0.27

